 "camp_letterman_features_printed": "Camp features: dead house, embalming tent, cookhouse, warehouse tent, cemetery of about 1,200 graves, amputated limbs buried in barrels and later sent to the Army Medical Museum.",
 "night_operations_B853": "Surgeons operated in the open on tables near the field, sometimes under tarpaulins, \"day and night\" until July 6 (July 7 for II Corps) (NPS-Essay5; Letterman-Exc). Spangler: four operating tables worked night and day under the barn forebay, lanterns burning (HN-Spangler; ReconEra; GExp). Weikert: amputated limbs piled outside a window; hospital moved east early July 3 (HN-Weikert). XII Corps: wounded removed, sheltered, fed and dressed within six hours; capital operations within 24 hours (Letterman-Exc). Rain: cold, constant rain July 4 (HN-Spangler). Plum Run overflowed and drowned some wounded in low ground (AMS).",
